    "sha": "a59204a448599abbf5e232eb2b1ab1004aa741e0",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKGE1OTIwNGE0NDg1OTlhYmJmNWUyMzJlYjJiMWFiMTAwNGFhNzQxZTA",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-20T23:43:06Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-20T23:43:06Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): judge a cross drill's first rapid from the turret index position\n\nOn a lathe or a mill-turn, the cross drill had no first-traverse law.\nThe lathe post positions C, then sends X and Z in one G00 from the\nturret's index position (the top of the X and Z travel). That rapid\ncan pass every radius from the first point out, at every height from\nit up. The new law `verify::live_first_traverse` reads the stock, the\nparts, the chuck and the tailstock revolved about the spindle in that\nband, and the cross branch refuses the drill by name when one reaches\nit. A mill-turn cross drill also answers to the upright law of its\ndefault mill post. The cross drill's stamp takes one more word.\n\nFixes #3077\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
